-- title:
--   Algebraicity of a point homomorphism generated by curves
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$, let $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ carry a relative group law $L$ (a functorial group structure on the sets $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ of $T$-points over each $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, compatible with base change) and satisfy the abelian-scheme property bundle (f smooth and proper, all fibres of the underlying map of $f$ over points of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ connected, and a relative group law exists), and likewise $f' : A' \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ with $L'$ and the same bundle. Let $h$ be a map from $k$-points of $A$ (sections of $f$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} k$) to $k$-points of $A'$ satisfying $h(L.\mathrm{mul}\,P\,Q) = L'.\mathrm{mul}\,(h P)\,(h Q)$. Let $C_i \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $i \in \{0,\dots,n-1\}$, be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, with $C_i$ integral, and let $\nu_i : C_i \to A$ be morphisms over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ such that every $k$-point of $A$ is the right-folded $L$-product, starting from $L.\mathrm{one}$, of a list of points $y_i$ followed by $\nu_i$, for some family of $k$-points $y_i$ of $C_i$. Assume further there are morphisms $w_i : C_i \to A'$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ with $h(y \text{ followed by } \nu_i) = y \text{ followed by } w_i$ for every $k$-point $y$ of $C_i$. Then there is a morphism $u : A \to A'$ with $u$ followed by $f'$ equal to $f$ such that every $k$-point $P$ of $A$ satisfies $P$ followed by $u$ equals $h(P)$. Nothing is asserted about $u$ being compatible with the group laws beyond this agreement on $k$-points.
--
--   This is the algebraicity criterion for a homomorphism between the groups of $k$-points of two abelian varieties: if it is induced by morphisms on a family of proper smooth integral curves whose iterated sum map is surjective on $k$-points, then it is induced by a morphism of schemes over $k$. It is used in the construction of the morphism realising a quotient of an abelian variety by a subgroup specified on points, in [`GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_hom_mapPt_eq_pointEquiv_symm_quotientMap_of_le_comap`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_hom_mapPt_eq_pointEquiv_symm_quotientMap_of_le_comap).
